  "profile": "https://lloom.dev/profiles/interchange/v1",
  "id": "linux-nvidia-dgx-spark-2x-glm53-atlas",
  "name": "2x DGX Spark GLM-5.3 Flash FP4-Local Atlas (SparkGLM 0.3.1, Enntity v80 drafter)",
  "version": 4,
  "summary": "Two directly connected Sparks running Atlas SparkGLM over the private fabric, serving nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-FP4-Local as published with 1048576-token contexts for four concurrent requests and Enntity v80 DFlash2-architecture speculative decoding. Additive only: no default model, no aliases overwritten.",
  "description": "This recipe installs SparkGLM 0.3.1 at the immutable product revision recorded in backends/atlas-sparkglm/pins-0.3.1-v80.json. LLooM owns orchestration, admission, worker-first startup, readiness, routing and telemetry. The Atlas engine image is built from Enntity/sparkglm by that repository's install/build.sh; LLooM commits no engine source. The engine (Atlas-Inf/atlas plus Enntity's open Atlas-Inf PRs, on the Enntity/atlas spark branch) is AGPL-3.0-only and runs from its own container image; the drafter is Enntity's v80 from a private repository. Setup acquires the pinned checkpoint and drafter and pulls the pinned image from GHCR by its immutable manifest digest (image.reference in the pin manifest; the mutable tag is never pulled); the serving path only ever starts the prepared image. nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-FP4-Local ships its MTP layer quantized, so the image serves the acquired checkpoint directly: there is no conversion step and no overlay. Each node verifies the pulled image by the io.enntity.sparkglm.install-tree contents label, arm64 architecture and the pinned engine commit; the label is a contents check, not the artifact identity. Explicit --source-build is only for users who want a local build from the pinned source, and it produces a LOCAL tag for an explicitly overridden local recipe, not the immutable recipe. The release includes structured output and tool calls plus image/video input; the release image qualified on 03/04 on 2026-11-03 against 0.3.0 (identical greedy output and prompt logprobs, 109/109 live checks; sparkglm-research experiments/qual-20261103).",
  "license": {
    "id": "MIT",
    "name": "Recipe metadata, launcher and orchestration"
  },
  "provenance": {
    "createdBy": "lloom",
    "generatedBy": "manual-curated",
    "source": "SparkGLM 0.3.1: Enntity/sparkglm 33fe02f83a9edf96ae38ebe4fc6a8ec8e7603f90 (tag v0.3.1, install tree e7af504a3dfde2652e05de9c32304ffd3de7f2fa), engine Enntity/atlas spark @ 5f79b46ba7b0e8b14f8b2966cca9e2546f18560d (Atlas-Inf main 2f9c37083, which carries Enntity's Atlas-Inf PRs #321, #322 and #323 and the maintainers' #319 and #320; AGPL-3.0-only, recorded in the image's /opt/atlas/source-manifest.json). The install pulls ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkglm@sha256:8e1e378b61f2633283fc86772b78f3524220255064630cc069d64b70cc5df7e0 by digest (pins-0.3.1-v80.json; the tag ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkglm:e7af504a3dfd is never pulled), and each host verifies the image's io.enntity.sparkglm.install-tree label, arm64 architecture and engine commit. Model nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-FP4-Local revision 76348ddb2be2e35e39ecfc00e75dc07703f4f3d5 (NVIDIA Open Model Agreement; base model MIT) is served as published, with no overlay; the Enntity v80 drafter Enntity/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2-enntity-v80 revision 8416cdfbf4cfb302b86a058cb5f5b89f891350c0 (DFlash2 architecture trained by Enntity, model.safetensors sha256 61190f81c66cbd0f; private repository, so each node needs a Hugging Face token with read access) is served from its checkpoint. The engine argument vector ships inside the image as /opt/atlas/profiles/4x1m.json, selected with SPARKGLM_PROFILE=4x1m, not in this recipe. The profile carries 1048576-token contexts, four sequences sharing one physical KV pool (GLM latent in FP8 with per-128 scales, split between the two nodes by SPARKGLM_KV_SHARD=1, about 2.6M tokens at the recipe's 0.91 GPU memory utilization with the display carveout, which overrides the profile default of 0.88, and shared with the disk prefix cache; the 48 GiB disk prefix-cache tier is enabled beside the shard, split into 24 GiB KV and 24 GiB SSM tiers per node), FP32 SSM state with KDA record rollback, and DFlash2 (gamma 8) on the head rank; disable-tool-grammar is deliberately not set so structured output and tools stay functional. Qualified on 03/04 on 2026-11-03: greedy output and prompt logprobs identical to 0.3.0, 109/109 live checks, speed level (sparkglm-research experiments/qual-20261103)."
  },
